/bin/
*.out
*.test
.DS_Store
.env

# Scan output. Client findings must never reach a public repository, so these
# patterns are a backstop, not the plan: write real assessment reports OUTSIDE
# the working tree entirely (see docs/assessment/runbook.md).
/report/
/report-*/
snapshot*.json

# The outreach tracker: prospect names, contacts and conversation notes. It is
# meant to live in ~/assessments/, never here - this is the backstop for a copy
# made into the tree by accident. The template it is copied FROM is committed
# (docs/assessment/tools/pipeline.csv.template) and holds no real data.
pipeline.csv
pipeline-*.csv

# `go build ./cmd/...` drops the binary here rather than in bin/
/ray-guard

# Integration-stack TLS fixture: generated by `make tls-fixture`, never
# committed. A security product does not ship private keys, test or otherwise.
/test/integration/fixtures/tls/
